# Line endings: LF everywhere, in the repository *and* in the working tree on
# every platform.
#
# Why eol=lf rather than plain text=auto: PRs #19 and #20 were both cut on
# machines that wrote CRLF into JOURNAL.md. main is LF, so not one line of a
# ~3000-line file aligned and git reported the entire file as a single conflict
# -- twice, on the same day, for changes that touched a few dozen lines each.
#
# text=auto alone normalises what gets *stored*. eol=lf also pins what gets
# *checked out*, which is the half that stops a Windows box or a CRLF-configured
# editor putting it straight back.
#
# This repo is documentation, one HTML page and two workflows. Nothing here
# needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.avif binary
